package org.mattshoe.mtg.core

internal val storyRavnica = StorySection(
    "ravnica", "Ravnica",
    "A city the size of a world kept its peace for ten thousand years with a single spell, and it has been paying for the day that spell broke ever since.",
    listOf(
        StoryArticle(
            "guildpact", "Guildpact",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "the-paruns", "The Paruns",
                    listOf(
                        "Before the city was a city, Ravnica was a world at war with itself. Its factions fought for centuries over the same streets and fields, and every peace was only a pause while the next war was gathered. Out of that exhaustion came a council of ten leaders, and at its head stood a lawmage remembered as Azor I, the first judge of what would become the Azorius Senate. He proposed something nobody had tried before, a treaty that was also a spell, a living enchantment that would enforce its own terms.",
                        "Not every faction wanted order. Some of the leaders at that table had built their power on chaos and saw a binding law as a cage. In the end all ten signed, in blood and magic, and each became a parun, the founder of a guild. Razia of the Boros set her name down second, after Azor. Svogthir of the Golgari signed third. The first draft, in Azor's own hand, still lies under thick enchanted glass in an Azorius library, and the year of the signing became year zero of the calendar Ravnicans would keep for ten thousand years.",
                        "One signature was kept out of the record. The tenth guild, House Dimir, was written into the pact in secret, and an amendment called the Hidden Charter made it a crime for any signatory to reveal that it existed. Its parun was {Szadek, Lord of Secrets}, the last of an ancient race of psychic vampires, a creature who would outlive almost everyone at that table. His guild had been handed the strangest duty in the whole treaty. Nobody at the signing could have guessed how much that duty would matter ten thousand years later.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "ten-guilds", "Ten Guilds",
                    listOf(
                        "The Guildpact did not keep the peace with soldiers. It worked through circumstance. A guild that reached into another guild's business found its plans going wrong in small and unlikely ways, a lost message, a missed meeting, a lucky accident for its rival, until the balance was restored. A Wojek officer arresting someone for breaking one of its laws could hold them with the pact's own magic, a seal that not even a parun could break.",
                        "Over the centuries the factions settled into their roles. The Azorius made and judged the law. The Boros kept order, and their League of Wojek patrolled the streets. The Izzet built and maintained the city's great works. The Golgari fed the city and took away its waste. The Orzhov ran its money and its oldest church. The Simic healed it, the Selesnya preached harmony and nature, and the Gruul kept what was left of the wild. Even the Rakdos had a written purpose. The founders bound the demon Rakdos to a cult of his own in the hope that a people to feed him would keep his murderous rages away from ordinary citizens.",
                        "Every guild got something from the arrangement, and every guildmaster spent the next ten millennia hunting for loopholes in it. About half the population belonged to no guild at all, but nobody on Ravnica lived outside the guilds' reach. The city grew until it covered the plane, one vast street map from horizon to horizon.",
                        "Once a year it all stopped. On the anniversary of the signing Ravnica held the {Festival of the Guildpact}, a day when weapons were laid down and the streets filled with drink and music. As the ten thousandth anniversary came near, the city prepared for the greatest festival in its history, the Decamillennial, when the Selesnya would perform a convocation meant to bless the entire plane. Somebody else was preparing too.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote(
                        "Everyone knows that violence at the Festival brings the worst of luck, so for at least one day a year arms are laid down in favor of brimming goblets.",
                        "Festival of the Guildpact",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-decamillennial", "The Decamillennial",
                    listOf(
                        "Lieutenant {Agrus Kos, Wojek Veteran} had served the League of Wojek for more than fifty years and preferred to work alone. On the eve of the Decamillennial he had a partner anyway, a young officer named Bell Borca, and a city swelling with pilgrims. Among them was Saint Bayul, a Selesnyan holy man coming into the city for the celebration with a ledev guard named Fonn. A bomb tore through the restaurant where they stopped. Borca died. Bayul was reported dead. Fonn vanished. Kos woke in a hospital, and soon his dead partner's ghost was holding him to an avenger contract.",
                        "Fonn had been taken by Jarad vod Savo, a Devkarin elf of the Golgari, who said he had been hired to save her from the blast. The job had come from his sister Savra, and then she sent harpies to kill them both. Kos pulled in old allies, the angel Feather and the Orzhov innkeeper Pivlic, and the investigation became a running fight across the city. The Golgari attacked the Boros headquarters. Selesnyan quietmen, silent soldiers who should have been keeping the peace, joined the fighting.",
                        "The design behind it was Savra's. {Savra, Queen of the Golgari} had corrupted Vitu-Ghazi, the Selesnyan city tree, and secretly controlled the quietmen. She meant to join the Selesnyan conclave using the gem set in Bayul's forehead, keep her grip on the Golgari, and reach for every guild after that. She had a partner. Szadek waited until she had joined the conclave, then snapped her neck and announced the end of the Guildpact.",
                        "It was Kos who stopped him. In the wreck of the ceremony the old lieutenant arrested the vampire for crimes against the Guildpact, the most natural thing a Wojek officer could do. The city survived its anniversary. Nobody understood yet that the arrest had done what Szadek could not.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "utvara", "Utvara",
                    listOf(
                        "Twelve years later Kos was working as a bouncer in a bar Pivlic had opened in Utvara, a ruined valley on the edge of the city that was being reclaimed from a sickness called the Kuga plague. Decades earlier an Izzet magelord named Zomaj Hauc had dropped a mana bomb on Utvara for an Orzhov patriarch known only as Uncle, meant to burn out the infected so the land could be taken back sooner. It went wrong. The blast tore a wound in the sky called the Schism, and the plague mutated instead of dying.",
                        "Uncle made his cousin {Teysa, Orzhov Scion} baroness of the valley and travelled out with her. He arrived dead, killed in what looked like a Gruul raid, and Teysa took up the work of making Utvara habitable before her contract handed it back to the Selesnya. She bought a cure for the plague from a Simic doctor. She also learned that her narcolepsy was a lie, that her servant Melisk had been wiping her memory, and that under his control she had killed Uncle herself so he could take a seat on the Obzedat, the Orzhov council of ghosts. She tore up her oath to the council.",
                        "Under the valley Hauc was hatching dragons. Funded by the Obzedat, he meant to overthrow {Niv-Mizzet, the Firemind} using three dragon eggs and ghostly energy drawn from the Schism. Teysa and Kos broke into his laboratory, the Cauldron, as the eggs woke. Hauc seized one dragon with a spell engraved on a goblin's metal arm, and Teysa seized the other by reciting the same spell from memory. The two beasts killed each other over Utvara. Hauc died against a cliff wall. Kos was impaled when his flying machine came down.",
                        "Agrus Kos looked up as he died and saw Feather, missing for years, come out of a glowing light that hung over the Schism. At his funeral Hauc's spirit woke and heard the voices of other spirits calling to him. The dead of Ravnica were not resting, and the reason was [the broken pact](the-breaking).",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Ravnica: City of Guilds"),
                StorySource("Set", "Guildpact"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Ravnica, by Cory J. Herndon"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Guildpact, by Cory J. Herndon"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Guildpact (spell)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Ravnica (novel)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Guildpact (novel)"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "the-breaking", "The Breaking",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "the-paradox", "The Paradox",
                    listOf(
                        "The grave did not get to keep Agrus Kos. The Azorius called his spirit back and set it inside the body of one of their ectomancers, Obez Murzeddi, because {Grand Arbiter Augustin IV} needed him. The Arbiter explained what had happened at the Decamillennial. When the [Guildpact](guildpact) was signed, Szadek's guild was given the duty of working against it, a counterweight that kept the other nine pulling together, much as the Rakdos supplied the chaos that made order necessary. A guildmaster could not lawfully be arrested for doing the job the pact had given him. Szadek knew that. He let his guard down so that Kos could take him, and in that moment the Dimir could no longer fulfil their part of the treaty.",
                        "The spell that had held Ravnica together for ten thousand years had simply stopped. Nobody had broken it by force. A good officer had done his duty.",
                        "The damage reached further than the streets. Feather stood trial for abandoning the Boros and told the Azorius court where the angels had gone. Their flying fortress, the Parhelion, had set out to learn why visitors from other worlds no longer came to Ravnica, and it had found Agyrem, a ghost world folded against the city like a blister, where Ravnica's dead went because they had nowhere else to go. The Schism over Utvara had snagged Agyrem and caught the Parhelion with it. Inside, the ghosts were at war with the angels.",
                        "When Feather finally reached {Razia, Boros Archangel}, the parun told her that she and Kos had broken the pact, and then Szadek's ghost appeared and killed her. Augustin told Kos that Szadek had escaped his cell and that only Kos could stop him. It was a tidy story. Very little the Grand Arbiter said that year was true.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "nephilim", "Nephilim",
                    listOf(
                        "In Utvara the wreck of Hauc's laboratory had woken something older than the pact. Five Nephilim, monsters from before the signing, fed on the last unhatched dragon egg and grew gigantic. Niv-Mizzet flew out to face them, killed two, took a little damage and withdrew, claiming to be bored. His own Izzet watched him go. The rest of the Nephilim walked toward the city.",
                        "Every guild seemed to be coming apart at once. The acting head of the Rakdos, {Lyzolda, the Blood Witch}, kidnapped a squad of young Selesnyan scouts, among them Myc, the son of Fonn and of Jarad, who was now guildmaster of the Golgari. She needed a guildmaster's blood and the brain fluid of a dragon, stolen from the Cauldron, to wake the demon Rakdos and take control of his body. Jarad broke into Rix Maadi to save his son. Lyzolda killed him, used his blood to finish the ritual, and the demon walked out into the streets.",
                        "The Simic had their own monster. Their guildmaster {Momir Vig, Simic Visionary} had spent years selling cytoplast grafts across the city, and every graft was a thread leading back to Experiment Kraj, a living weapon built to absorb all of them. Vig meant to set Kraj on Rakdos in public and show Ravnica who ruled it. Kos, riding first a Simic virusoid and then the corpse of Savra, which the old Golgari god Svogthir had been wearing, got close enough to kill Vig before he could take control.",
                        "Kraj broke loose, tore through Novijen, fought Rakdos and swallowed the demon into its own body, leaving him in a coma and itself unmoving. Lyzolda felt every wound and collapsed, and her own cultists ate her. Two guildmasters were dead and a third was sealed inside a monster, and all of it had been arranged.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote(
                        "Of course it will grow beyond control—it was designed to choose its own evolution.",
                        "Momir Vig, Experiment Kraj",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "augustins-plot", "Augustin's Plot",
                    listOf(
                        "The Senate met in a Prahv half wrecked, because the Parhelion had come out of Agyrem and crashed into it. A motion was made to give Augustin martial law over the whole plane, and it was seconded. Kos arrived to object. While he bent the senators' minds so they saw something else, the Grand Arbiter finally told him the truth.",
                        "Szadek had never escaped. When the vampire was brought to the Azorius cells after the Decamillennial, Augustin finished off his ancient rival and took control of his ghost. He sent the ghost into Agyrem to raise the dead against the angels, and he had counted on Kos to speed the collapse by killing another guildmaster, which Kos had done in Novijen. Augustin wanted a new Ravnica where everyone followed the law because there was nothing else left to follow.",
                        "Kos and his friends ran for the Parhelion and sabotaged its engine. On the bridge he caught Szadek's spirit in a grounder, a trap for ghosts. As they fled he hurled it at Augustin. Szadek burst out of the broken trap, recognized the man who had enslaved him, and pulled his soul out of his body. Then the Parhelion exploded.",
                        "Two years later {Feather, the Redeemed} led the Boros, and a new Azorius guildmaster brought Kos back, still a ghost but with a body of his own instead of borrowed ones. The Schism faded, and Agyrem settled over Ravnica as a new quarter of the city, with Szadek loose somewhere inside it. Kos took command of the Boros there. Above him the guilds signed a new accord, which turned out to be worth exactly what it cost.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-interregnum", "The Interregnum",
                    listOf(
                        "Teysa Karlov drafted the new accord, and on paper it was a fine document. It had no magic behind it, and no guild took it seriously. For the first time in ten thousand years nothing stopped a guild from reaching into another's business except other guilds, and the city's patience with its masters ran out. The guildless, half of Ravnica, had spent millennia living under duties fixed by a spell. The spell was gone and the guilds' worst habits were not. In time the guilds were officially disbanded, and many of their halls were torn down by the people they had ruled.",
                        "Agyrem lingered over the city until [the Mending](the-mending), when the ghost world dissolved and the spirits trapped in it could finally pass on.",
                        "It was in these years that a young telepath from another world settled in. [Jace](who/jace) Beleren lived well in the upper city by reading the secrets of the rich and charging them for his silence, and it was on Ravnica that the Infinite Consortium found him and its master Tezzeret recruited him. To most Ravnicans he was just another face in the crowd, which was what he liked about the place.",
                        "The guilds did not stay dead. Habit and tradition proved nearly as strong as the pact. One by one they came back, many under new leaders, some with new purposes now that no spell held them to the old ones. They came back without a referee, and the old feuds resumed with nothing to temper them. Then strange symbols began turning up all over the Tenth District, and the Izzet League started measuring them with great interest. [Azor's last law](implicit-maze) was waking up.",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Dissension"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Dissension, by Cory J. Herndon"),
                StorySource("Novel", "Agents of Artifice, by Ari Marmell"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Dissension (novel)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Szadek"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Ravnica"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "implicit-maze", "Implicit Maze",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "strange-marks", "Strange Marks",
                    listOf(
                        "[Jace](who/jace) Beleren came back to Ravnica after some bad years to find the Infinite Consortium collapsed without him, and found he did not care. What caught him was a puzzle. Strange symbols and patterns were turning up all over the Tenth District, and the Izzet League was very interested in them. With a vedalken archivist named Kavin, Jace set out to work out what they were, and the work turned into an obsession.",
                        "His friend {Emmara Tandris} of the Selesnya came looking for him when he disappeared into his notes. She gave him a small wooden pendant, offered him a place in the Conclave and asked for his help. He turned down the place. He was not the only one watching the Izzet, either. House Dimir, which most of Ravnica believed long gone, had noticed him.",
                        "Jace tracked {Ral Zarek} and his crew back to the Izzet Guildgate and found Niv-Mizzet himself waiting there. With the chance slipping away, he reached into the dragon's mind. He got his answers, and the Firemind's attention along with them. Kavin wanted no part of what they had learned. Jace agreed to walk away and, to make it stick, erased six months of his own memories of the work.",
                        "While he was doing it, the Cult of Rakdos abducted Emmara. Jace woke with a hole in his past, his friend gone and the Azorius coming for him. He had to learn everything again, with less time and more enemies.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "lost-months", "Lost Months",
                    listOf(
                        "The Azorius lawmage Lavinia had come to arrest him, and Jace slipped away with help from Ruric Thar, a Gruul ogre he had apparently hired to wreck his own sanctum. His only clue led to a Rakdos nightclub and the blood witch Exava. He escaped with a location torn from a cultist's mind and followed a leyline into Golgari territory, where the Golgari warrior Varolz found him and Emmara saved him. Then the Dimir vampire Mirko Vosk struck. He wounded Emmara badly and tore through Jace's mind, only to find nothing there worth stealing.",
                        "At Vitu-Ghazi the Selesnya welcomed Emmara home and threw Jace out after he accused her companion Calomir of not being who he claimed to be. Jace fought Ruric Thar in a Gruul ring to win back what the ogre knew, and turned a Rakdos riot back into its own territory with a towering illusion of the demon. None of it won him the maze. Niv-Mizzet gave it to everyone. The dragon made an announcement across the district that revealed nearly every secret Jace had worked so hard to learn twice.",
                        "Exava cornered him in the chaos. He was rescued by {Lazav, Dimir Mastermind}, the shapeshifting master of the Dimir, who carried him into the undercity, explained a surprising amount of his plans and then handed him back to Vosk. Jace planeswalked out of the Dimir prison, but not before Vosk pulled the route of the maze out of his mind as Jace tried to send it to Emmara. He woke on Zendikar and seriously considered never going back.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-bailiff", "The Bailiff",
                    listOf(
                        "A kor family on Zendikar changed his mind, and Jace returned to Ravnica to start at the end. In the Forum of Azor, where the maze finished, he met the Bailiff, a being made of law and bound to the place. Azor had carved the maze into the foundations of the city as a contingency. If the [Guildpact](guildpact) ever dissolved, its leylines would surface and set the guilds a test. If they ran it together, a new Guildpact would be made. If they did not, the Bailiff would deliver Azor's {Supreme Verdict}.",
                        "Jace followed Lavinia to a meeting where Isperia, the sphinx who led the Azorius, explained the verdict to a disguised Lazav. It was a spell that could destroy all the guilty in a district. Jace understood what that meant. The maze was a trial and the guilds were the accused. If they ran it as rivals, Azor's law would wipe them out before their quarrels could destroy the plane.",
                        "Niv-Mizzet had decreed that each guild would send one champion, and on the appointed day they gathered at the {Transguild Promenade}. Jace found Emmara, now the Selesnya runner, and told her what he had learned. When the race began, the two made it through the Selesnya and Golgari gates together. At the Azorius gate Lavinia finally arrested him.",
                        "Isperia herself heard the case. Jace explained everything and pleaded guilty to save time. His sentence was community service, helping the champions finish the maze. He went back in after Emmara.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-race", "The Race",
                    listOf(
                        "The champions were Lavinia for the Azorius, Tajic for the Boros, Mirko Vosk for the Dimir, Varolz for the Golgari, Ruric Thar for the Gruul, Teysa Karlov for the Orzhov, Exava for the Rakdos, Emmara for the Selesnya and Vorel for the Simic. The Izzet runner was a researcher named Melek, until Ral Zarek took his place. Each guild wanted the prize for itself. Nobody but Jace had read the fine print.",
                        "Jace passed the Dimir and Orzhov gates and found Emmara fighting Teysa. He turned the Orzhov envoy's servants on one another, which backfired when they turned on Teysa instead and she wiped them out herself. So he bought her delay with the rest of the route, and he and Emmara went on through the Simic gate to the Izzet gate. Ral was waiting there. He told Emmara that Jace was a planeswalker, and her trust in him broke. Then Ral tried to kill him with everything he had prepared. Jace survived on an illusion and went on alone.",
                        "At the Forum of Azor all ten champions had arrived and were attacking one another. Jace stopped them for a moment, and Lazav set them at each other again. The Bailiff saw a trial being failed and delivered the verdict by giving every runner the power to cast it. Any one of them could now end all ten guilds. {Maze's End} had become a courtroom with ten executioners in it.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "living-guildpact", "Living Guildpact",
                    listOf(
                        "Jace reached into all ten minds and joined them, so that each runner could see straight into the others. Nobody cast the verdict. Holding that many minds began to unravel his own, and the Bailiff stepped in to ease the weight. In doing so it declared Jace the new Guildpact, the mediator who could understand every guild's side. The old treaty's magic returned, living in a man. Any law {Jace, the Living Guildpact} affirmed aloud now bound the guilds as the pact once had.",
                        "Days later Emmara kissed him in thanks and asked him to take away her memories of other worlds and planeswalkers. She could not keep such a secret from her guild and still do her duty. With regret, he did as she asked.",
                        "The trouble was that the Living Guildpact was a planeswalker, and planeswalkers leave. Jace kept rushing back, and Lavinia kept the office running while he was gone, but each time he left the guilds went back to fighting over scraps. Vraska, a gorgon planeswalker from the Golgari undercity, tried to manipulate him into her power. Niv-Mizzet set Ral to find out where Jace kept vanishing to, and chasing that question the two of them found another planeswalker who appeared near the Boros garrison at the same hour every day, [Gideon](who/gideon) Jura. Jace would leave Ravnica with him and help found [the Gatewatch](gatewatch).",
                        "Ravnica needed its referee at home, and he was almost never there. Someone far older than the guilds had noticed that, and was already buying guildmasters. When [Nicol Bolas](who/nicol-bolas) finally came, [he came for the whole city](ravnica-war-of-the-spark).",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Return to Ravnica"),
                StorySource("Set", "Gatecrash"),
                StorySource("Set", "Dragon's Maze"),
                StorySource("Novel", "The Secretist, Parts One to Three, by Doug Beyer"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Implicit Maze"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Jace Beleren"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Living Guildpact"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "ravnica-war-of-the-spark", "War of the Spark",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "new-guildmasters", "New Guildmasters",
                    listOf(
                        "[Nicol Bolas](who/nicol-bolas) did not invade Ravnica first. He bought it, one guild at a time. When Niv-Mizzet disappeared, Ral Zarek took over the Izzet League. {Kaya, Orzhov Usurper}, a planeswalker who could kill ghosts, was hired to destroy the Obzedat, and through a loophole in Orzhov law every debt the council held fell onto her shoulders and made her guildmaster. Vraska murdered the Golgari guildmaster Jarad and took the Swarm. Domri Rade beat Borborygmos in a duel for the Gruul. Dovin Baan, a vedalken from Kaladesh, rose to a leading place in the Azorius Senate. Each of them had made some bargain with the dragon.",
                        "Not all of them stayed bought. Ral, Kaya and Vraska each came to see what the dragon was, and they began to work against him with Lavinia of the Azorius and Hekara, the Rakdos emissary. Their plan depended on a fail-safe in the old magic. With all ten guilds agreeing, they could make Niv-Mizzet the new Living Guildpact, with the power of the pact behind him. [Jace](who/jace) was off the plane again, and Ravnica needed a guardian who stayed.",
                        "Getting ten guilds to agree on anything had defeated Azor himself. Ral spent weeks being refused by every guild in turn. In the end there was only one thing left to try. Isperia called a summit at New Prahv.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-summit", "The Summit",
                    listOf(
                        "At the {Guild Summit} Isperia proposed a radical idea, cooperation. The talk was bitter and every guild had members who opposed it. Then Niv-Mizzet arrived and told the guildmasters what they were really facing, an elder dragon from beyond their world. He offered to leave the Izzet and stand above the guilds as Ravnica's guardian if they would make him the Living Guildpact. Many of them did not trust him. The summit adjourned until morning.",
                        "That night {Vraska, Golgari Queen} met Isperia alone in the conference chamber. Bolas had demanded the sphinx's death, and Vraska had her own grudge against the Azorius, who had once jailed her. She turned Isperia to stone. In the morning the guildmasters found the statue, and every guild suspected every other. Isperia's death opened the way for Dovin Baan to take the Azorius.",
                        "Niv-Mizzet tried to fight Bolas without the pact and was killed. Hekara was murdered. Vraska fled to Ixalan ahead of Ral's fury. With nothing else left, Ral switched on the {Interplanar Beacon}, a device grown out of Izzet research that would call planeswalkers from across the Multiverse to Ravnica, and at that same moment Bolas arrived.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote(
                        "In a climate of suspicion, Isperia gathered the guilds to propose a radical idea: cooperation.",
                        "Guild Summit",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-dreadhorde", "The Dreadhorde",
                    listOf(
                        "The planeswalkers who answered the Beacon found they could not leave. Dovin switched on the Immortal Sun, an artifact Bolas had taken from Ixalan, and it pinned every planeswalker to the plane. In the Tenth District Plaza a citadel and a statue of the dragon rose. Tezzeret opened the Planar Bridge inside the Chamber of the Guildpact, and the blast tore apart the leylines beneath it. Jace lost the pact's power on the spot.",
                        "Through the bridge came the Dreadhorde, armies of undead Eternals from [Amonkhet](amonkhet), led by [Liliana](who/liliana) Vess. They killed civilians in the streets without distinction, because dead civilians drew planeswalkers out. The Boros and the Dimir declared against Bolas. Ral led the Izzet into battle and brought the Simic with him. Kaya talked the Orzhov elite into fighting, though they despised her for forgiving debts. Under Aurelia and Feather the Boros counterattacked behind the floating fortress {Parhelion II}, with [Gideon](who/gideon) Jura beside them, and for a while it worked.",
                        "Nissa Revane woke Vitu-Ghazi, the great city tree of the Selesnya, and walked it into the plaza to topple the dragon's statue, and the city's defenders took heart. Bolas answered with his God-Eternals, the undead gods of Amonkhet, and they tore the tree to pieces. The Boros fell back. Then Bolas cast {The Elderspell}, and his Eternals began harvesting sparks. Domri Rade, who had sworn himself to Bolas, was the first planeswalker drained and killed.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote(
                        "With the harvest of Domri's spark, the Elderspell began to fuel Bolas's ascension to godhood.",
                        "Spark Harvest",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-ritual", "The Ritual",
                    listOf(
                        "The trapped planeswalkers met with Ravnica's leaders and split into teams. Kaya went with two young planeswalkers, Teyo Verada and Araithia Shokta, to win over the guilds that had stayed out of the fight, the Selesnya, the Gruul, the Golgari and the Rakdos. Ral joined them. Vraska came back. So did Hekara, raised from death. Lazav took the shape of [Chandra](who/chandra) Nalaar to draw off Dovin while the real Chandra shut down the Immortal Sun, and Lazav left the vedalken blinded and fleeing. With Dovin gone, Lavinia could bring the Azorius in.",
                        "For the first time since the summit, all ten guilds stood together. Nissa and the guild representatives performed the ritual, repairing the leylines the bridge had broken and bringing Niv-Mizzet back from death as the new Living Guildpact. The dragon rose as {Niv-Mizzet Reborn} and used his first moments of that power to burn the God-Eternal Kefnet to nothing, and the effort knocked him unconscious.",
                        "The last assault on the citadel cost more. Gideon gave his life taking Liliana's demonic contract onto himself so that she could turn on Bolas, and she did. When the dragon reeled, it was the revived Niv-Mizzet who drove the god Hazoret's spear into his back, and a God-Eternal who finished the work. How the dragon's plan came apart is told in [the other half of this story](bolas-war-of-the-spark). On the ground, Ravnicans counted their dead.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-reckoning", "The Reckoning",
                    listOf(
                        "Vitu-Ghazi was splinters. The Chamber of the Guildpact was a ruin. Whole blocks of the Tenth District had been fought over street by street, and hundreds of planeswalkers had died with their sparks torn out, along with Ravnicans beyond counting. Domri was dead. So was Dack Fayden, the thief. The city held a {Planewide Celebration} anyway, and Kaya joined the Gatewatch.",
                        "Niv-Mizzet and the guildmasters did not forget who had let the dragon in. Ral, Kaya and Vraska were set to atone by hunting down Bolas's other servants, Ral after Tezzeret, Vraska after Dovin Baan and Kaya after Liliana. Many Ravnicans drew a simpler lesson, that planeswalkers brought ruin with them whatever their intentions, and they would hold onto it.",
                        "The city had barely begun to rebuild when the second blow came. In [the Phyrexian invasion](invasion-of-the-multiverse), a compleated Vraska led the attack on her home plane, aimed it first at New Prahv and the jail that had once held her, and had Ravnicans blinded and left to crawl through streets slick with oil. The Golgari were converted almost entirely. Ral drove her forces back with a weapon tuned against the oil, and the guilds held on with the Guildpact's power behind them. The second Chamber of the Guildpact fell too.",
                        "When the oil dried, Ravnica's balance was gone. Distrust ran deep, and the guilds that had survived were hollowed out. What came next began with a party, and a body, in the [Karlov family's manor](karlov-manor).",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Guilds of Ravnica"),
                StorySource("Set", "Ravnica Allegiance"),
                StorySource("Set", "War of the Spark"),
                StorySource("Novel", "The Gathering Storm, by Django Wexler"),
                StorySource("Novel", "War of the Spark: Ravnica, by Greg Weisman"),
                StorySource("Story", "March of the Machine, Ravnica: One and the Same, Magic Story on magic.wizards.com"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: War of the Spark (event)"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Ravnica"),
            ),
        ),
        StoryArticle(
            "karlov-manor", "Karlov Manor",
            listOf(
                StoryTab(
                    "after-the-oil", "After the Oil",
                    listOf(
                        "A year after [the invasion](invasion-of-the-multiverse), Ravnica was still out of balance. The Golgari had been almost entirely compleated, the Dimir were rumored to be gone, and nobody trusted the Simic or the Izzet, who had been caught studying the oil when they should have been fighting it. Niv-Mizzet, the Living Guildpact since [the war with the dragon](ravnica-war-of-the-spark), had reaffirmed himself as the city's supreme authority. Some guilds were stretched thin, their ranks emptied by the invasion. Others had turned inward and all but stopped doing the jobs the [Guildpact](guildpact) gave them. Many Ravnicans blamed planeswalkers for both disasters.",
                        "So the guildless started doing the work themselves, patrolling streets and repairing what the guilds had let fall. The most important of their new institutions was the Ravnican Agency of Magicological Investigations, led by an archon named Ezrim, and in a city where crime was climbing, its detectives kept a kind of peace.",
                        "In the Orzhov, {Teysa, Opulent Oligarch} had taken the guild back from Kaya while Kaya was off defending the Multiverse. Kaya had kept her spark, and her visits put the guilds on edge. Teysa summoned her home anyway, to stand for the Orzhov at a celebration at Karlov Manor attended by representatives of every guild but the Golgari, and privately chided her for failing to protect Ravnica during the invasion. Kaya wondered whether Teysa was right.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-party", "The Party",
                    listOf(
                        "Kaya met dignitaries, and a young Agency inspector named Kellan. Then Zegana, the leader of the Simic, was assassinated in the middle of the party. The Agency sent its best, {Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth}, a former Azorius lawmage with a perfect memory and a mind that missed nothing. With Kaya's help he quickly exposed Etrata, a Dimir assassin who had attended in secret, and she was arrested. She swore she was innocent. She remembered nothing of the murder.",
                        "Three days later Kaya returned to the manor and found Teysa dead too. Beside the body was a note scrawled in Phyrexian, in Teysa's own hand. Ezrim asked Kaya to lead the investigation, and she took Kellan on as her assistant. Proft, who did not believe Etrata had killed anybody, broke her out of Azorius custody so she could help him prove who had.",
                        "So the case split into two trails across the city. One belonged to a ghost hunter and an inspector, the other to a detective and the assassin he had arrested. {Etrata, Deadly Fugitive} had every reason to run. She stayed, because the only way to clear her name was to find the real killer.",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "two-trails", "Two Trails",
                    listOf(
                        "Kaya and Kellan questioned Judith of the Rakdos, who sent them to the original Guildpact, now kept in a museum at Vitu-Ghazi. What it said about the Rakdos pointed at the demon himself. On the way back a gang of thugs attacked them, and when the thugs lost, they swallowed pills that turned their bodies to moss before anyone could question them. At headquarters Teysa's killer had been found, a guildless man with no memory of the deed. Aurelia arrived with Massacre Girl in tow, who had tried to kill the Boros guildmaster in the same blank state, and gave Kaya twenty-four hours before the Legion went to war with the Rakdos.",
                        "Proft and Etrata followed their own trail. In the safehouse where Etrata had spent the night before the party, they found a yellow-gray powder on her bed. Massacre Girl, hired by Judith, tried to kill Proft. Kylox, an Izzet scientist who might have explained the powder, was snatched by Krenko's goblins, then stabbed to death by a man who burst through a window meaning to kill Krenko and who remembered nothing afterward. Izoni of the Golgari told them the powder came from a living thing not native to Ravnica.",
                        "Then everything happened at once. Anzrag, a Gruul god held in Agency evidence, broke loose and rampaged through headquarters. {Agrus Kos, Spirit of Justice}, the old Wojek ghost from [the Decamillennial](guildpact/the-decamillennial), went missing, taken by Judith so the blame would fall on Rakdos while she seized the cult for herself. Aurelia was done waiting. A message brought Kaya to Karlov Cathedral, where Teysa's funeral was being prepared, and Proft was there. She gave him three things he had not had, the Phyrexian note, the attempt on Aurelia and the thugs who turned to moss. He told her he knew who the killer was.",
                    ),
                    quote = StoryQuote(
                        "Eventually I'll give retirement another shot. But not today.",
                        "Agrus Kos, Spirit of Justice",
                    ),
                ),
                StoryTab(
                    "the-accusation", "The Accusation",
                    listOf(
                        "Proft gathered the guild leaders in Trostani's private study inside Vitu-Ghazi and announced he would question them one at a time. He took Kaya into a side room first, and they sat in silence until a flower pushed up through the floor. As it was about to release its pollen, Kaya cut the stem, and Proft sealed it in an Agency capsule before it could wither. The questioning had been bait. He had made himself a target, and chosen Kaya because a brainwashed planeswalker could simply leave after killing him.",
                        "Everyone involved had lost their memory just before their crime and recovered it just after. The pollen did not grow naturally on Ravnica, but it could have been cultivated, and it showed none of the marks of Phyrexian work. It could not work on the same person twice, or Etrata would have been made to kill again. It was a powerful plant with careful limits, the work of someone who could command nature and respected it. And the roots of Vitu-Ghazi ran under the whole city.",
                        "Tolsimir Wolfblood stepped forward to confess. Proft refused him. The killer was {Trostani, Three Whispers}, or rather Oba, the central dryad of the three, punishing those she saw as traitors to Ravnica during the invasion. Zegana had experimented with Phyrexian oil. Teysa had served as a double agent who looked like a collaborator. Krenko had profited. Oba lashed out with the city tree's vines, and Kaya, Etrata and Teysa's own ghost trapped her in an Agency ward until her sisters put her to sleep.",
                        "At the funeral Teysa's spirit came to take back the Orzhov, and advised Kaya to leave Ravnica for a while so the succession would stay clear. Kaya went. Proft kept Etrata on as his aide and pulled the last loose thread, Kylox's research, which led straight to Niv-Mizzet and a plan to control the [Omenpaths](the-omenpaths) opening across the plane.",
                    ),
                ),
            ),
            listOf(
                StorySource("Set", "Murders at Karlov Manor"),
                StorySource("Story", "Murders at Karlov Manor, by Seanan McGuire, Magic Story on magic.wizards.com"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Murders at Karlov Manor"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Alquist Proft"),
                StorySource("Reference", "MTG Wiki: Kaya"),
            ),
        ),
    ),
)
